    "narrative": "The **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** tandem anchor the Austin Waves lineup today, offering the highest projected ceilings against favorable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the premier play at 83.29, benefiting from a soft matchup against Bailey Ober (xERA 4.78) and a significant situational boost from Ober\u2019s slow delivery, which increases the likelihood of a stolen base\u2014a critical factor for our 5x5 objectives. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.82) finds himself in a high-leverage spot against Patrick Sandoval; his combination of elite power and a favorable platoon advantage makes him our most reliable source of R and RBI production today. **Luis Robert Jr.** (75.65) and **Jacob Wilson** (72.73) also command attention, with the latter seeing his value inflated by a 19% SP skill adjustment against Nick Martinez, providing a much higher floor than his base projection suggests.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Nasim Nunez**, whose speed profile typically keeps him in consideration, but he ultimately fell short with a 48.11 rating against Shota Imanaga. While **Nasim Nunez** provides the SB utility we prioritize, the high efficiency of our starting outfielders\u2014specifically **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker**\u2014pushed him to the pine. We are also closely monitoring the weather in the game featuring **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci**; both carry a 33% rain risk. While **Miguel Vargas** maintains a solid 63.34 score due to his high xwOBA and favorable matchup against Nick Lodolo, any weather-related delay could complicate our daily efficiency targets. We will keep **Jackson Merrill** (38.94) in reserve, as his poor matchup against the sharp Kyle Harrison (xERA 2.92) makes him a liability in this specific slate.",
